Iteration notes:
- Initial Expressltexx configuration rejected an attempted CONFIG_SSBI=y;
  these kernels build ssbi.o under MFD_PM8XXX. Removed the nonexistent symbol.
- Source review found native Expressatt MDP4's explicit RPM fabric bandwidth
  dependency. Added INTERCONNECT, INTERCONNECT_QCOM, and
  INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8960=y, rebuilt successfully, and asserted the final
  generated .config (not merely the TOML). Its DT supplies mdp0-mem/mdp1-mem;
  drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp4/mdp4_kms.c:373 documents FIFO underruns without
  the vote. A regression test now covers these symbols.
- Both final configs have CONFIG_KEXEC=y and CONFIG_SMP unset. Source evidence
  for SMP=n is arch/arm/kernel/machine_kexec.c:machine_kexec_prepare and
  arch/arm/mach-qcom/platsmp.c's missing cpu_kill. This removes a kernel-side
  barrier; it does not implement or validate userspace ARM32 handoff.

